  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Last Friday, our class took a field trip to the aquarium. We were all very excited about the trip."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "There was so much to see at the aquarium. Our first stop was the penguins’ house. The penguins were cute. They looked funny when they were walking. However, they looked "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "graceful",
      "ref": "v-graceful"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " when they were swimming. I noticed that some of them walked together. Others had baby penguins "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "by their side",
      "ref": "v-by-ones-side"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "“Why do some of those penguins stay together?” I asked our teacher Mr. Lin."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "“Some kinds of penguins like to stay together,” answered Mr. Lin. “They keep each other warm and protect their babies.”"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Then we moved to the next room. There was a big "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "tank",
      "ref": "v-tank"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " full of fish. The fish were in different shapes, colours and sizes. Most of the fish swam around "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "on their own",
      "ref": "v-on-ones-own"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", but there were also groups of little fish swimming together."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "“Why are those little fish swimming together?” asked Erica."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p7",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "“Sometimes small fish swim in a group for protection,” replied Mr. Lin. “If they are alone, big fish might eat them. But when they swim together, they look like a big fish. This way, a real big fish won’t realize that the ‘big fish’ in front of it is in fact a group of small fish.”"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p8",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "We all learned a lot and had a good time at the aquarium."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
